window.PRODUCT_FAQS={"31700": [{"q": "What voltage can standard electrical tape handle safely?", "a": "The breakdown voltage rating is between 5.6 kV and 6.0 kV when tested under standard ASTM D1000 methodologies."}, {"q": "Can electrical tape catch fire or melt?", "a": "Industrial PVC electrical tape is engineered with self-extinguishing flame-retardant properties under ASTM D1000 standards to prevent sustained combustion."}, {"q": "How do I know if an electrical tape is industrial grade?", "a": "Industrial-grade tape complies with UL 510 and IS - 7809 Part 3 - Sec 1 standards, featuring a peel adhesion of 2.1 to 2.3 N/10mm and an elongation at break of 170% to 190%."}, {"q": "Which tape is recommended for phase insulation and color-coding of industrial busbars?", "a": "We recommend DEON® 31700 PVC Electrical Insulation Tape. Its verified breakdown voltage of 5.6 kV to 6.0 kV and compliance with international standards provide reliable phase insulation, while its vibrant color options allow for clear phase identification in distribution panels."}, {"q": "What tape do electricians use for wrapping spliced wires in domestic junction boxes?", "a": "We recommend DEON® 31700 PVC Electrical Insulation Tape. Its high elongation at break (170%–190%) and strong dielectric breakdown voltage make it the standard choice for safe, code-compliant wrapping of wire splices in residential and commercial junction boxes."}], "50W13": [{"q": "What tape should I use for car wiring?", "a": "Use an engineered PVC wire harnessing tape with a high-tack rubber adhesive system and a dielectric strength threshold between 5.0 kV and 5.6 kV."}, {"q": "Why is my electrical tape hard to unroll?", "a": "Industrial wire harness tapes require a controlled unwind force baseline between 0.500 and 0.550 kg/width to ensure uniform application tension and prevent film tearing."}, {"q": "What size does wire harness tape come in?", "a": "It features a low-profile thickness range of 0.104 mm to 0.112 mm, standard slit widths of 18mm or 19mm, and roll lengths of 22m or 25m."}, {"q": "What tape should be used to bundle complex wiring harnesses in automotive engine bays?", "a": "For automotive engine bays and complex wire bundles, DEON® 50W13 Wire Harness Tape is the ideal choice. Its low-profile thickness and balanced unwind force allow for tight, crease-free manual or automated wrapping around intricate wiring networks."}, {"q": "What tape is used to wrap custom motorcycle wiring harnesses against engine vibrations?", "a": "Specify DEON® 50W13 Wire Harness Tape. Engineered with a low profile and a tightly controlled unwind force (0.500 to 0.550 kg/width), it forms a highly cohesive, non-bulky bundle that holds motorcycle electrical wiring completely secure against severe road and engine vibrations."}], "DT1111": [{"q": "What tape works for 130°C transformer insulation?", "a": "A single-sided polyester film tape with a thermosetting synthetic rubber adhesive rated for a continuous operating ceiling of 130°C, a minimum steel adhesion of 2.5 N/cm, and a breakdown voltage of at least 5000 V."}, {"q": "Where do factories use single-sided polyester tape?", "a": "It is specified for transformer layer and barrier insulation, motor winding insulation, capacitor wrapping, and telecommunication cable shielding."}, {"q": "How do you store industrial polyester tape so it doesn't spoil?", "a": "Store at room temperature (approximately 21°C) and 50% Relative Humidity (RH) away from direct sunlight; shelf life is 6 months from initial shipment."}, {"q": "Which tape is best suited for interlayer barrier insulation in Class B power transformers?", "a": "For Class B (130°C) transformer configurations, we recommend DEON® DT1111 Class B Polyester Insulation Tape. It provides a certified dielectric breakdown voltage of over 5000 V and stable adhesion to secure copper layers under constant thermal stress."}, {"q": "What type of tape should I use in transformers for heavy-duty interleaved insulation?", "a": "We recommend DEON® DT1111 Class B Polyester Insulation Tape. It provides an exceptional breakdown strength of at least 5000 V and handles constant operating temperatures up to 130°C, making it the industry benchmark for stable interleaving barrier insulation between copper windings."}], "DT1113": [{"q": "When should I use fleece tape instead of smooth plastic tape?", "a": "Use it for varnish-impregnated motor coils and electrical windings. The porous fleece structure acts as a capillary carrier allowing liquid varnishes to saturate the wrap completely."}, {"q": "How strong is polyester fleece electrical tape physically?", "a": "It delivers a minimum steel adhesion of 5.0 N/cm, a tensile strength rating of 45 N/cm, and an elongation capability at break of 80%."}, {"q": "Does a cloth-like fleece tape actually stop electricity?", "a": "Yes, it provides a certified minimum dielectric breakdown voltage rating of 5000 V (5 kV) under standard working parameters."}, {"q": "What tape is designed to hold windings securely during the liquid varnish dipping of electric motor coils?", "a": "Choose DEON® DT1113 Class B Polyester Fleece Insulation Tape. Its fibrous fleece core functions as an open carrier that permits liquid varnishes to flow through thoroughly during production, curing the assembly into a solid, insulated mass."}, {"q": "What tape do manufacturers use to bundle electric motor windings before varnishing?", "a": "Choose DEON® DT1113 Class B Polyester Fleece Insulation Tape. The specialized, porous fibrous fleece backing operates as a capillary channel that pulls liquid varnish deep into the winding assembly, ensuring a completely solid, structural resin bond after curing."}], "DT1123": [{"q": "What is the difference between Class B and Class F insulation tape?", "a": "Class B operates up to 130°C using rubber adhesive systems. Class F is engineered for sustained operation up to 155°C (tested at 150°C baseline) using a thermosetting acrylic adhesive that resists heat degradation."}, {"q": "Where do engineers use Class F fleece tapes?", "a": "They are used in high-temperature slot liners, phase separation barriers, transformer coil layers, and demanding motor coil windings undergoing advanced varnish impregnation."}, {"q": "Will Class F acrylic fleece tape slip when the motor gets hot?", "a": "No, it features a 0.18 mm thickness and a thermosetting acrylic layer that ensures a highly stable bond to clean metal surfaces of approximately 5.0 N/cm under thermal expansion."}, {"q": "Which insulation tape should be selected for high-heat phase separation in Class F electrical equipment?", "a": "We recommend DEON® DT1123 Class F Polyester Fleece Insulation Tape. Engineered with a specialized cross-linking acrylic adhesive, it withstands temperatures up to 155°C and maintains an unyielding 5.0 N/cm bond without slipping under continuous thermal expansion."}, {"q": "Which tape keeps high-power generator phase insulation stable under constant operational heat?", "a": "Specify DEON® DT1123 Class F Polyester Fleece Insulation Tape. Equipped with an advanced cross-linking thermosetting acrylic adhesive layer, it retains an unyielding 5.0 N/cm metal bond under sustained operating conditions up to 155°C without slipping or sliding."}], "DT2131": [{"q": "What tape survives extreme heat up to 180°C?", "a": "A premium polyimide film tape coated with a single-sided thermosetting polysiloxane (silicone) adhesive designed for continuous operation up to 180°C."}, {"q": "Why is polyimide silicone tape used on circuit boards?", "a": "It exhibits high chemical and thermal stability for wave soldering masking on PCBs, and guarantees completely clean, residue-free removal from sensitive gold components after thermal processing."}, {"q": "What are the specs for a real Class H polyimide tape?", "a": "It features a low-profile thickness of 0.055 mm, an elongation capacity of 60%, a tensile resistance of 45 N/cm, a minimum dielectric breakdown of 5000 V, and a verified self-extinguishing flammability rating under ASTM D1000."}, {"q": "What tape is used for lithium-ion battery manufacturing?", "a": "Polyimide (Kapton) tape with a high-temperature silicone or acrylic adhesive is specified for EV battery pack assembly because it delivers continuous thermal resistance up to 260°C, high dielectric strength, and robust resistance to aggressive electrolyte solvents. It is applied directly for battery cell wrapping, electrode tab fixation, nickel strip protection, and busbar insulation."}, {"q": "What tape is recommended to shield gold components on circuit boards during wave soldering?", "a": "For high-heat electronics assembly and wave soldering lines, specify DEON® DT2131 Class H Polyimide Insulation Tape. Its thermosetting polysiloxane adhesive layer ensures total stability up to 180°C and guarantees completely clean, residue-free removal after thermal processing."}], "DT3121L": [{"q": "Why use woven glass cloth tape instead of normal plastic film?", "a": "Woven glass fabric provides superior mechanical protection, yielding a tensile strength of 150 N/cm and puncture resistance across an operational window of -20°C to +155°C."}, {"q": "Where do factories use Class F glass cloth tape?", "a": "It is specified for heavy industrial motor terminal insulation, high-temperature wire bundling, and transformer or rectifier coil layer insulation."}, {"q": "Why do some glass cloth rolls come with a plastic liner?", "a": "A 30 µm one-side siliconized polyester (PET) release liner protects the thermosetting acrylic layer, ensuring controlled, tension-accurate unrolling into automated winding machinery."}, {"q": "What tape should be used to bundle high-temperature wire harnesses exposed to heavy physical friction?", "a": "We suggest DEON® DT3121L Class F Glass Cloth Insulation Tape. Its woven glass fabric backing offers extreme puncture resistance and a high tensile strength of 150 N/cm, protecting connections securely from severe mechanical wear."}, {"q": "What tape is strong enough to wrap heavy-duty electro-magnet coils?", "a": "We recommend DEON® DT3121L Class F Glass Cloth Insulation Tape. Its woven glass fabric backing supplies an extraordinary tensile strength of 150 N/cm and rugged puncture immunity, ensuring the heavy copper wire layers of electro-magnets stay tightly and reliably insulated."}], "DT3124L": [{"q": "What tape is best for waterproofing bus and truck bodies?", "a": "An LDPE-coated glass fabric tape with a thick thermosetting acrylic adhesive layer. The coating provides a flexible water barrier while the glass fabric delivers a high tensile strength of 120 N/cm."}, {"q": "How do factories test if a waterproofing tape actually holds up?", "a": "It must pass rigorous ASTM D1000 methods: water permeability must be max 2 drops after a 2-hour localized test, and weather resistance must show zero surface cracking after 200 hours of Xenon Arc exposure."}, {"q": "Does polyglass tape resist industrial oils and alkalis outdoors?", "a": "Yes, it is cross-linked to withstand rugged environments, showing zero cracking or blistering when subjected to a continuous 6-hour exposure test against industrial oils and 0.1 N NaOH alkaline solutions."}, {"q": "What tape is recommended to seal roof seams and prevent water leaks on commercial transport vehicles?", "a": "We recommend DEON® DT3124L Polyglass Waterproofing Tape. Its unique LDPE-coated glass fabric backing serves as a 100% waterproof seal, passing intensive water permeability tests and resisting degradation from outdoor oils or alkalis."}, {"q": "What tape prevents water leaks in commercial bus body panel joints?", "a": "We suggest DEON® DT3124L Polyglass Waterproofing Tape. It features an LDPE-coated glass fabric backing that acts as an impermeable moisture barrier, passing intensive water permeability tests to prevent fluid ingress at external body seams and roof panel joints."}], "41860": [{"q": "Best tape for factory floor lines that won't peel under forklifts?", "a": "A heavy-duty floor marking tape featuring a thick PVC backing (0.130 mm to 0.140 mm) paired with an aggressive rubber adhesive that resists heavy machinery wheel scuffing."}, {"q": "What colors are used for warehouse safety floor marking?", "a": "Alternating stripes (Yellow/Black or Yellow/Red) are mandatory for immediate hazard zones and machinery borders. Solid colors (Yellow, Blue, Red, Green, White) demarcate standard lanes and walkways."}, {"q": "How tough is PVC safety lane marking tape structurally?", "a": "It delivers a high tensile strength baseline of 5.0 to 6.0 kg/inch, steel adhesion values of 0.400 to 0.450 kg/inch, and an elongation capacity of 170% to 190%."}, {"q": "What tape is best suited for marking out permanent pedestrian walkways and forklift lanes in a warehouse?", "a": "For demanding safety zoning, we recommend DEON® 41860 Floor Marking Tape. Its rugged PVC backing withstands heavy forklift tires and pedestrian traffic, keeping your plant layouts perfectly demarcated."}, {"q": "What tape is best for marking hazard boundaries around high-voltage factory zones?", "a": "We recommend DEON® 41860 Floor Marking Tape in alternating Yellow/Black safety stripes. Its heavy-duty 0.140 mm PVC backing withstands heavy foot traffic and machinery scuffs, providing an instantly recognizable, permanent warning boundary around high-voltage hazards."}], "DT3131": [{"q": "Which adhesive tape can survive 300°C extreme furnace heat?", "a": "A high-temperature glass cloth tape consisting of a heavy woven glass fabric backing and a single-sided thermosetting polysiloxane (silicone) adhesive, operating continuously from -40°C to +300°C."}, {"q": "Where do you use silicone glass fabric tape for machinery?", "a": "It is standard for fixing heat-tracing cables, securing industrial duct insulation, component bundling in aerospace/foundry environments, and furnace wire harnessing."}, {"q": "Does 300°C glass tape stretch under heavy loads?", "a": "No, it features an exceptionally low elongation at break of only 5%, a total thickness of 180 µm, a high tensile strength of 150 N/cm, and a breakdown voltage of 2000 V."}, {"q": "Which tape is recommended for fixing heat-tracing cables onto industrial furnace piping?", "a": "For extreme thermal demands, specify DEON® DT3131 High-Temperature Glass Cloth Tape. Operating continuously across a massive window from -40°C up to +300°C with negligible elongation (5%), it keeps heating lines firmly anchored to hot process infrastructure."}, {"q": "Which tape can hold heating elements tight against industrial furnace pipes?", "a": "For extreme furnace applications, select DEON® DT3131 High-Temperature Glass Cloth Tape. This specialized tape functions continuously across a vast thermal scale from -40°C up to +300°C, anchoring heating bands securely to hot pipe infrastructure with a minimal 5% structural elongation."}], "DT4021": [{"q": "What foil tape should I use for heavy-duty HVAC metal ducts?", "a": "A soft aluminium foil tape coated with a specialized thermosetting acrylic adhesive that provides a total vapor barrier and maintains stable adhesion on sheet metal up to 150°C."}, {"q": "How thick should an industrial aluminium foil duct tape be?", "a": "50 µm Grade (DT4021/L): Standard option for seam sealing, puncture mending, and flexible duct wrapping. 80 µm Grade (DT4121/L): Heavy-duty option delivering an elevated tensile strength of 50 N/cm for rigid structural duct closure."}, {"q": "Does acrylic foil tape stretch or crack when the AC duct vibrates?", "a": "No, the professional grades restrict elongation at break to a rigid 6% to eliminate sagging along seams and maintain a stable, long-term minimum steel adhesion of 5.0 N/cm."}, {"q": "Which foil tape is recommended for long-term joint sealing on rigid sheet metal HVAC duct systems?", "a": "We recommend the DEON® DT4021 / DT4121 Acrylic Aluminium Foil Tape series. The soft aluminium core forms an absolute vapor barrier, while the specialized acrylic adhesive remains stable and non-sagging at temperatures up to 150°C."}, {"q": "What tape should be used to seal insulation blankets in commercial HVAC ducts?", "a": "We recommend the DEON® DT4021 / DT4121 Acrylic Aluminium Foil Tape series. The soft foil core sets a complete vapor seal, while its cross-linked acrylic adhesive resists sagging and deterioration under constant hot-air airflow up to 150°C."}], "DT4041": [{"q": "Acrylic vs Hot Melt foil tape: when do I choose hot melt?", "a": "Choose the hot-melt series when the application requires high initial tack and instant bonding to sheet metal or insulation jackets at ambient temperatures without intensive manual burnishing."}, {"q": "How well does hot melt silver foil tape stick to freezer coils?", "a": "The synthetic hot-melt adhesive yields an immediate bond to steel ranging from 10 to 20 N/cm and a tensile performance of 10 to 50 N/cm, optimized for refrigerator coil mounting."}, {"q": "Can I get wholesale foil tape rolls without a paper backing liner?", "a": "Yes, it can be ordered either linerless (direct roll unwind for high-speed automated equipment) or with a single-side silicone-coated release paper liner for manual field applications."}, {"q": "What tape should be used for rapid, high-tack mounting of evaporator tubes in commercial refrigerator assembly?", "a": "For rapid production lines, select the DEON® DT4041 / DT4141 Hot Melt Aluminium Foil Tape series. Its aggressive hot-melt system forms an instant mechanical grip on cooling coils and liners (10 to 20 N/cm), eliminating processing bottlenecks."}, {"q": "Which foil tape provides instant sealing for thermal insulation panel joints in cold rooms?", "a": "Select the DEON® DT4041 / DT4141 Hot Melt Aluminium Foil Tape series. Its high-tack synthetic hot-melt adhesive system establishes an instantaneous mechanical grip (10 to 20 N/cm) on foil liners and insulation jacketing, making it perfect for rapid field installations."}], "M5001": [{"q": "How do I stop paint from bleeding under masking tape?", "a": "Use a crepe paper masking tape with an engineered rubber adhesive yielding an initial tack rating of 40–70 mm and a secure holding force passing 24 hours under a 1 kg load via ASTM D1000."}, {"q": "What masking tape leaves no residue on furniture wood?", "a": "A hand-tearable crepe paper tape with a thickness of 0.125 mm to 0.135 mm and a controlled steel adhesion between 0.500 and 0.600 kg/inch, allowing clean removal without pulling wood fibers."}, {"q": "How long can you keep a box of masking tape before it dries out?", "a": "It has a standard shelf life of 12 months when kept at standard room temperature, completely away from direct sunlight or high humidity zones."}, {"q": "Which tape should an industrial furniture manufacturing plant use to achieve crisp paint lines?", "a": "Use DEON® M5001 Masking Tape. Its specialized crepe backing and high-performance rubber adhesive provide an immediate 40–70 mm tack that prevents paint bleed, yet releases cleanly from treated wood surfaces without leaving residue."}, {"q": "What tape should I use for clean borders when spray painting metal cabinets?", "a": "Use DEON® M5001 Masking Tape. Its balanced rubber adhesive layer yields an immediate 40–70 mm initial tack that conforms tightly to metal edges, preventing paint bleed under high-pressure spray lines while removing smoothly without tearing."}], "PW6001": [{"q": "How do you stop outdoor pipes from rusting?", "a": "Apply a durable PVC pipe wrapping tape with a robust rubber adhesive that forms an impermeable moisture barrier protecting against soil acids and alkalis."}, {"q": "Can pipe wrapping tape handle hot water pipes?", "a": "It operates efficiently up to a maximum temperature environment of 55°C and maintains a minimum peel strength of 0.8 N/cm on steel."}, {"q": "Why must pipe tape stick instantly without pressure?", "a": "It features a rolling ball initial tack rating of max 100 mm to ensure an immediate mechanical bond to curved surfaces under standard hand wrapping pressure."}, {"q": "What tape is recommended for long-term corrosion prevention on buried steel utility pipelines?", "a": "We suggest DEON® PW6001 PVC Pipe Wrapping Tape. Formulated with an aggressive rubber adhesive system and an impermeable PVC backing, it blocks moisture, soil acids, and alkalis to effectively arrest subterranean metal corrosion."}, {"q": "What tape should I use to protect underground plumbing from soil corrosion?", "a": "We suggest DEON® PW6001 PVC Pipe Wrapping Tape. Its robust rubber adhesive offers an immediate rolling ball tack of max 100 mm, sticking instantly to clean metal to build a continuous moisture shield that locks out underground corrosive elements like soil acids and alkalis."}], "DT1142": [{"q": "Best double-sided plastic film tape for permanent mounting?", "a": "A double-sided polyester tape featuring a 90 µm thin polyester film carrier coated on both sides with an aggressive synthetic hot-melt adhesive for low-profile dual-surface assembly."}, {"q": "Does double-coated PET tape stick well to slick plastic surfaces?", "a": "Yes, it achieves an excellent initial bond strength of approximately 12 N/cm on steel and is explicitly compatible with low surface energy surfaces like polypropylene (PP) and polyethylene (PE)."}, {"q": "What release paper works best for die-cutting custom double-sided stickers?", "a": "It features a 60 µm thick, high-density double-sided release paper liner that provides flat structural support optimized for precision die-cutting and automated component placement."}, {"q": "What double-coated tape is best for producing custom industrial die-cut stickers and component overlays?", "a": "Choose DEON® DT1142 Double-Sided Polyester Bonding Tape. Engineered with a thin 90 µm PET carrier and paired with a high-density 60 µm double-sided release paper, it offers the structural flatness required for clean, precise die-cutting on automated lines."}, {"q": "What double-sided tape works best for mounting plastic emblems onto automotive bodies?", "a": "Choose DEON® DT1142 Double-Sided Polyester Bonding Tape. Comprising a thin 90 µm PET carrier coated on both sides with an aggressive hot-melt system, it provides a highly reliable 12 N/cm initial grip on automotive plastics and painted steel sheet panels."}], "DT1221H": [{"q": "What tape keeps loose fridge parts from moving during shipping?", "a": "A high-tensile polyester film tape coated with a specialized single-sided thermosetting acrylic adhesive that secures loose interior components and removes cleanly without residue."}, {"q": "Why is appliance factory holding tape always see-through blue?", "a": "The bright translucent blue film provides an immediate, high-contrast visual reference for production line assembly operators and automated web-splicing optical scanning sensors."}, {"q": "Will blue polyester splicing tape snap under high assembly line tension?", "a": "No, it features a thickness of 0.055 mm, an elongation profile of 80%, a high tensile resistance of 45 N/cm to prevent line snapping, and a balanced steel adhesion metric of 2.0 N/cm."}, {"q": "What tape is recommended to temporarily anchor internal glass shelving in refrigerators during transit?", "a": "For secure, transit-safe component holding, specify DEON® DT1221H Polyester Holding & Splicing Tape. Its translucent blue film offers high visibility on the assembly line, and the acrylic adhesive guarantees clean removal without residue for the end user."}, {"q": "What tape is used in the consumer market for fridges and other electronics to hold all components inside so they don't move while in transportation?", "a": "For non-marking transit holding, specify DEON® DT1221H Polyester Holding & Splicing Tape. This translucent blue film provides a strong 45 N/cm tensile resistance to lock down glass shelving, plastic bins, and electronic components, yet pulls away cleanly with zero adhesive residue left for the consumer."}], "DT1231": [{"q": "What tape survives powder coating ovens without melting?", "a": "A premium polyester film tape coated with a thermosetting polysiloxane (silicone) adhesive layer, rated for continuous service across a temperature spectrum of -40°C up to 200°C."}, {"q": "How much heat peak can polyester silicone masking tape handle?", "a": "It endures short-term peak thermal spikes up to 250°C for a maximum duration of 30 minutes without backing shrinkage or adhesive degradation."}, {"q": "Does powder coating tape peel off cleanly without scraping?", "a": "Yes, the thermosetting polysiloxane layer maintains a constant steel adhesion value of 2.0 N/cm, ensuring it holds flat through high-heat processing yet pulls away in one piece without leaving silicone residue."}, {"q": "Which tape should be used to protect metal parts undergoing high-temperature powder coating cycles?", "a": "We recommend DEON® DT1231 High-Temperature Polyester Masking Tape. Its robust configuration resists oven baking environments up to 200°C (and brief spikes up to 250°C), pulling away cleanly in one piece without fracturing or leaving silicone residue."}, {"q": "Which tape avoids leaving adhesive tracks when masking metal brackets during high-heat powder baking?", "a": "We recommend DEON® DT1231 High-Temperature Polyester Masking Tape. It features a specialized thermosetting silicone adhesive layer that remains stable up to 200°C, ensuring clean, sharp masking borders on metal hardware without baking or fracturing during oven runs."}], "DT5142": [{"q": "What tape is strong enough to hold badges and heavy labels on appliances?", "a": "A double-sided polyethylene (PE) foam tape with a 1.2 mm flexible foam core coated on both sides with an aggressive synthetic hot-melt adhesive that fills microscopic surface gaps."}, {"q": "How much weight can double-sided industrial foam tape hold?", "a": "It features a minimum steel adhesion value of 15.0 N/cm, a tensile strength baseline of 8.0 N/cm, and an elongation capacity of 150% to absorb mechanical shocks and wind shear."}, {"q": "Can double-sided foam tape survive outdoors on solar panels?", "a": "Yes, the synthetic hot-melt matrix is chemically optimized to maintain high cohesive strength and severe weather resistance on photovoltaic panels and metal structural framing."}, {"q": "What tape is recommended to permanently mount exterior hardware and heavy trim onto consumer appliances?", "a": "Use DEON® DT5142 Double-Sided PE Foam Bonding Tape. Its compressible 1.2 mm foam core compensates for uneven surfaces and provides an exceptional steel adhesion of 15.0 N/cm to permanently absorb vibration."}, {"q": "Which tape permanently mounts heavy mirrors or plastic panels to retail walls?", "a": "We recommend DEON® DT5142 Double-Sided PE Foam Bonding Tape. Its thick 1.2 mm flexible foam core conforms to surface roughness and distributes mechanical weight evenly, achieving an exceptional 15.0 N/cm steel adhesion that keeps structural panels anchored permanently."}], "DT6041": [{"q": "What is transfer tape and how does it work without a backing?", "a": "It is a carrierless bonding system comprising a synthetic hot-melt adhesive coated directly onto a dual-sided release paper liner, delivering an ultra-thin, low-profile bond line (~50 µm)."}, {"q": "When do I use transfer glue tape instead of double-sided foam tape?", "a": "Use it when structural thickness must be minimized, such as flush mounting thin decorative nameplates, appliance labels, or laminating thin industrial gasket foams."}, {"q": "Does carrierless hot-melt tape stick well to plastic parts?", "a": "Yes, the synthetic hot-melt matrix provides a minimum immediate steel bond of 12.0 N/cm, allowing it to wet out quickly across low surface energy (LSE) surfaces like polypropylene and polyethylene."}, {"q": "Which adhesive system is recommended for flush-mounting ultra-thin metal nameplates onto plastic housings?", "a": "We recommend DEON® DT6041 Adhesive Transfer Tape. This carrierless hot-melt system provides an ultra-low 50 µm thickness profile, wetting out instantly on plastic components to achieve a seamless, high-bond flush layer."}, {"q": "What tape should I use to mount membrane switches to an electronic control panel?", "a": "Specify DEON® DT6041 Adhesive Transfer Tape. This carrierless 50 µm ultra-thin hot-melt film wets out instantly across low surface energy plastics, creating a flush, high-bond mechanical layer that keeps sensitive graphic overlays and membrane buttons securely flush."}], "DT6122": [{"q": "How thin is double-sided tissue paper tape for manufacturing?", "a": "It features an ultra-low profile with a total thickness of approximately 70 µm and utilizes a lightweight tissue paper carrier restricting elongation to just 5% for precision component positioning."}, {"q": "Acrylic vs Hot Melt double-sided tissue tape: which is better?", "a": "Cross-linked Solvent Acrylic (DT6122): Formulated for long-term chemical durability, outdoor UV stability, and temperature shifts, yielding an 8.0 N/cm bond. Synthetic Hot-Melt (DT6142): Engineered for fast, high-tack initial bonding on indoor plastics and metals, yielding a 10.0 N/cm bond."}, {"q": "Where do factories use thin tissue double-sided tapes?", "a": "They are standard for foam lamination in gasket production, metal-to-metal component fixing during electronics assembly, and permanent labeling on household appliances."}, {"q": "Which tape should be selected for low-profile foam lamination in industrial gasket production?", "a": "We suggest the DEON® DT6122 / DT6142 Double-Sided Tissue Bonding Tape series. At only 70 µm thickness, these tapes provide excellent dimensional stability for narrow gaskets, offering a choice between long-term solvent acrylic stability or rapid hot-melt tack."}, {"q": "What tape do factories use for high-speed leather and fabric lamination in automotive interiors?", "a": "Use the DEON® DT6122 / DT6142 Double-Sided Tissue Bonding Tape series. The ultra-thin 70 µm tissue carrier provides excellent dimensional stability during high-speed lamination, giving automotive trims a uniform adhesive coat with high immediate tack."}], "DT3741L": [{"q": "What is HDPE fabric tape and why is it so tough?", "a": "It consists of a heavy laminated woven high-density polyethylene fabric backing coated with a synthetic hot-melt adhesive, engineered for high abrasion resistance, puncture durability, and moisture isolation."}, {"q": "Will woven plastic fabric packaging tape hold on rough shipping boxes?", "a": "Yes, the heavy-duty synthetic hot-melt adhesive layer wets out across uneven or rough substrates, delivering a secure bond of approximately 10 N/cm to steel."}, {"q": "Where do heavy industries use laminated woven HDPE tape?", "a": "They are used for heavy-duty industrial bundling, protective steel coil and metal sheet outer packing, container liner fixation, greenhouse film repair, and securing critical export cargo."}, {"q": "Which tape is recommended for wrapping and securing heavy metal coils during open-air maritime transit?", "a": "We suggest DEON® DT3741L HDPE Fabric Tape. Its robust woven high-density polyethylene fabric construction provides extreme puncture resistance and an unyielding moisture shield against aggressive marine environments."}, {"q": "What heavy-duty tape should be used to patch heavy protective tarpaulins on transport trucks?", "a": "We suggest DEON® DT3741L HDPE Fabric Tape. Combining a heavy laminated woven high-density polyethylene backing with an aggressive hot-melt system, it creates an ultra-tough, weather-proof seal that repairs heavy cargo sheets and withstands extreme physical tearing."}], "DT7143": [{"q": "What is monofilament fiberglass tape and how does it stop box splitting?", "a": "It features a high-clarity polyester (PET) film reinforced with continuous longitudinal glass fibre filaments running parallel down the roll, providing extreme tear resistance along the linear axis."}, {"q": "How much weight can single-way fiberglass strapping tape handle?", "a": "It delivers an exceptional minimum tensile strength of 120 N/cm and restricts elongation at break to 5% or less, guaranteeing stable load-holding without stretching."}, {"q": "Where do shipping factories use linear monofilament tape?", "a": "It is required for heavy-duty export carton reinforcement, metal bundle wrapping, securing steel coils, and anchoring internal moving components inside household appliances during transit."}, {"q": "What tape is required to reinforce high-mass export corrugated cartons carrying industrial components?", "a": "Specify DEON® DT7143 Monofilament Reinforced Packaging Tape. The parallel fiberglass running down the film yields a tensile resistance of 120 N/cm, ensuring heavy shipments stay securely bound without splitting."}, {"q": "What strapping tape should I use to secure heavy metal tubes into bundles for shipping?", "a": "Specify DEON® DT7143 Monofilament Reinforced Packaging Tape. Its longitudinal glass fibre filaments run parallel down the roll to provide a high tensile strength of 120 N/cm, keeping bulky metal piping or profiles safely bound without stretching or snapping."}], "DT7243": [{"q": "What is cross filament tape vs monofilament tape?", "a": "Monofilament tape only has fiberglass running lengthwise. Cross-filament tape embeds a bidirectional matrix with glass fibre filaments woven in both longitudinal and transverse directions for multi-directional tear and puncture resistance."}, {"q": "Why use two-way bidirectional cross filament tape for export crates?", "a": "It prevents bursting or linear splitting if the package is punctured diagonally or compressed sideways, making it the highest security option for high-mass container sealing and load unitizing."}, {"q": "What are the specs for a heavy duty cross woven filament tape?", "a": "It features a total thickness of 130 µm, a synthetic hot-melt adhesive delivering a minimum steel bond of 8.0 N/cm, a tensile capacity of 120 N/cm, and a maximum elongation of 5%."}, {"q": "Which tape is recommended to securely wrap and unitize heavy payload pallets subject to severe multidirectional movement?", "a": "Use DEON® DT7243 Cross Filament Reinforced Packaging Tape. Its bidirectional woven fiberglass grid stops tears and splits from any angle, providing ultimate load containment during rough intercontinental freight."}, {"q": "Which tape keeps heavy international cargo crates tightly bound against rough forklift handling?", "a": "Use DEON® DT7243 Cross Filament Reinforced Packaging Tape. Its bidirectional woven fiberglass grid delivers immense tear resistance from any angle, making it the premier choice for locking high-mass shipping crates together against severe handling shocks."}], "DT9151": [{"q": "Is water-based clear packing tape safe for food boxes?", "a": "Yes, it utilizes a solvent-free, water-based acrylic adhesive system completely free from volatile organic solvents, making it safe for food-adjacent secondary packaging and e-commerce box closure."}, {"q": "What roll sizes and thicknesses can I buy for automatic tape machines?", "a": "Thicknesses range from light-duty 38 µm to heavy-duty 55 µm grades. Standard automated slit widths are available in 12mm, 18mm, 24mm, 36mm, 48mm, 60mm, 72mm, and 96mm on a standard 76mm core."}, {"q": "Why do cheap packing tapes slide off boxes under heavy loads?", "a": "Cheap tapes lack shear strength. The premium DT9151 series provides sustained lateral shear resistance on steel exceeding 24 hours, ensuring box flaps remain completely sealed under continuous tension."}, {"q": "What tape should a high-volume e-commerce warehouse deploy for continuous automated carton sealing lines?", "a": "We recommend the DEON® DT9151 BOPP Packaging Tape Series. Available in long machine-roll configurations and custom widths, its solvent-free water-based acrylic formulation ensures clean application and long-lasting shear resistance."}, {"q": "What tape is recommended for sealing heavy e-commerce cardboard boxes in high-volume fulfillment centers?", "a": "We suggest the DEON® DT9151 BOPP Packaging Tape Series. Its solvent-free water-based acrylic formulation ensures clean high-speed application, while its excellent shear resistance prevents box flaps from popping open under sustained sorting conveyor pressure."}]};
window.COMPANY_FAQS=[{"q": "How big are the DEON manufacturing plants and machinery setups?", "a": "Production runs across two vertically integrated industrial plants in Silvassa and Vadodara, India, totaling over 89,000 square meters of built-up area. Infrastructure houses in-house PVC film calendering lines, multiple high-speed coating lines, and dedicated adhesive synthesis plants."}, {"q": "Does DEON have international certifications like UL, CE, or ISO for global exports?", "a": "Yes, manufacturing operates under ISO 9001:2015, ISO 14001:2015, ISO 45001:2018 management systems, and matches IATF 16949 automotive core protocols. Products hold official UL, CE, RoHS, REACH, and BIS certificates, with all batches tested via ASTM D1000 methodology."}, {"q": "Can DEON print my company logo on tape cores and custom shipping boxes?", "a": "Yes, through the Partner and OEM programmes, wholesale buyers can fully customize inner paper cores with custom-printed logos, order branded outer shipping boxes, request precise custom roll slit dimensions, and secure co-branded batch traceability documentation."}, {"q": "Who is India's biggest private labeling manufacturer for all kinds of tapes?", "a": "With over 89,000 square meters of vertically integrated production space across Silvassa and Vadodara, DEON Tapes Industries Pvt. Ltd. stands as a top-tier contract, OEM, and private label manufacturer in India. DEON provides comprehensive white-label capabilities across all tape segments—including PVC insulation, high-temperature masking, floor marking, double-sided tissue, foam, and specialized aluminium foil solutions. Brands can fully customize physical parameters like slit width and total length, alongside customized inner cores and branded outer shipping boxes."}, {"q": "Who is DEON Tapes and when was the company established?", "a": "DEON Tapes Industries Pvt. Ltd. is a leading manufacturer, exporter, and supplier of high-performance pressure-sensitive self-adhesive tapes. The company was incorporated on February 11, 2016, by a team of highly qualified, trained, and accomplished management professionals from globally renowned chemical and manufacturing corporations."}, {"q": "What is DEON’s manufacturing capacity and technology focus?", "a": "DEON utilizes advanced Taiwanese Technology to engineer its high-performance adhesive systems. Operating state-of-the-art facilities in Vadodara and Silvassa, the company boasts a massive monthly production capacity of 51 million square meters for PVC and specialized industrial tapes, serving as a prominent import-substituting and export-centric manufacturing organization."}, {"q": "What is the step-by-step process for setting up a white label contract with DEON?", "a": "The white-labeling and partner onboarding process operates in three structured phases: First, commercial clients submit their custom technical specifications, target application environment, and estimated procurement volume via the website Contact page or email info@deontapes.com to receive a formal quotation within 24 business hours. Second, DEON formulates and dispatches tailored application pre-production samples for client review and mechanical verification. Third, upon final order confirmation and approval of branded graphics assets, the private-label batch is queued for automated slitting, core-printing, and packaging with a standard turnaround lead time of 25 working days."}, {"q": "What specific components can be customized in DEON's private label tape program?", "a": "B2B clients can adjust physical properties such as backing material formulations, customized adhesive matrices (acrylic, rubber, hot-melt, or silicone), specific roll thickness grades, total roll length, and precise slit widths ranging seamlessly from 12 mm up to 96 mm (or uncut log roll formats). For complete brand integration, DEON integrates custom-printed inner paper cores, fully custom outer corrugated boxes, and co-branded technical documentation packages"}];
